siteconf -i [-P web] [-SB=build] [-Osite_url=...]   # writes ./configure
./configure [-DB=outdir] [-Db=reldir] [-Ovar=val]    # MY/config.mk, MY/option.mk
siteconf -g [-B outdir] [-G make|ninja]             # Makefile or build.ninja, MY/MANIFEST.*
cd ${B} && make [goal]

MANIFEST:
    MAKE all
        NEED file1      # relative to ${a}; made as ${B}/${b}/file1
        WANT file2      # soft: resolved into MY/MANIFEST.all
    MAKE small
        NEED file1

Headers (HAVE/NEED/WANT in any comment style, REM and :: too): paths
from the project root, spelled in full:
    # HAVE: ${A}/${a}/index.html     ${A} is always "."
    # NEED: ${B}/${b}/style.css      a generated file: made first
    # NEED: skel/HTML                bare names are from the root
${b} is relative to ${B}; on its own it is an error.

In templates (TT2): D.* (config.mk), O.* (option.mk), location
(reversed from HAVE declaration), locate(...).  ./configure and
./render are generated deterministically (provided the same flags
are passed), so it's possible to keep local changes in a patch.

Tests: ./env.pl prove -r gengenlib/t genlib/t template-provider/t siteconf/t
